Attach (recommended) or Link to PDF file here: N/A

Configuration:
- Web browser and its version: N/A
- Operating system and its version: N/A
- PDF.js version: `master`, or any version after PR #17563
- Is a browser extension: N/A

Steps to reproduce the problem:
1. Apply the following diff
```diff
 diff --git a/web/firefoxcom.js b/web/firefoxcom.js
index 07d9f73e0..eb453b27a 100644
--- a/web/firefoxcom.js
+++ b/web/firefoxcom.js
@@ -407,6 +407,9 @@ class FirefoxExternalServices extends DefaultExternalServices {
   }

   static async getNimbusExperimentData() {
+    if (!PDFJSDev.test("GECKOVIEW")) {
+      return null;
+    }
     const nimbusData = await FirefoxCom.requestAsync(
       "getNimbusExperimentData",
       null
```
2. Run `gulp mozcentral`.
3. Look at the `build/mozcentral/browser/extensions/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs` and `build/mozcentral/browser/extensions/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs` files.

What is the expected behavior? (add screenshot)
That the `getNimbusExperimentData`-methods look like
```js
  static async getNimbusExperimentData() {
    return null;
  }
```
respectively
```js
  static async getNimbusExperimentData() {
    const nimbusData = await FirefoxCom.requestAsync("getNimbusExperimentData", null);
    return nimbusData && JSON.parse(nimbusData);
  }
```

What went wrong? (add screenshot)
Deadcode elimination not working as intended
```js
  static async getNimbusExperimentData() {
    if (true) {
      return null;
    }
    const nimbusData = await FirefoxCom.requestAsync("getNimbusExperimentData", null);
    return nimbusData && JSON.parse(nimbusData);
  }
```
respectively
```js
  static async getNimbusExperimentData() {
    if (false) {}
    const nimbusData = await FirefoxCom.requestAsync("getNimbusExperimentData", null);
    return nimbusData && JSON.parse(nimbusData);
  }
```

Link to a viewer (if hosted on a site other than mozilla.github.io/pdf.js or as Firefox/Chrome extension): N/A

